  "live_records": {
    "q-108563": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108563",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix above. Find its decomposition using Jordan blocks.",
      "worked_solution": "Our matrix can be represented as the composition of three Jordan blocks (one $2\\times 2$ block and two $1\\times 1$ blocks), as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]={J}_{2}(5)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(3)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(3)\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
