    "q-108569": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108569",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${J}_{1}(-2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}(\\pi )=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, recall the following:\n\n- ${J}_{1}(-2)$ represents a $1\\times 1$ Jordan block with $-2$'s on the leading diagonal,\n\n- ${J}_{2}(\\pi )$ represents a $2\\times 2$ Jordan block with $\\pi $'s on the leading diagonal.\n\nTherefore, our Jordan blocks are given by\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(-2)=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\end{aligned}],\\,{J}_{2}(\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}\\pi  & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\pi \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe composition of our Jordan blocks gives the following block diagonal matrix:\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(-2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}(\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\pi  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\pi \\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-108569-a",
              "type": "math",
